./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2620:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:560:> Throughput workloads (compilers, render farms) will perform **worse** than CFS/EEVDF. This scheduler explicitly trades throughput for latency — the same tradeoff network CAKE makes for packets.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2621:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:562:### Comparison with Other sched_ext Schedulers
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2622:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:564:| Feature                 | scx_cake                            | scx_bpfland                    | scx_lavd                       | scx_cosmos                        |
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2623:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:577:> scx_cake is **not** a general-purpose scheduler. It makes explicit tradeoffs that benefit gaming at the cost of throughput workloads. For daily desktop use without gaming, `scx_bpfland` or `scx_cosmos` may be better choices.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2624:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:587:| **CAKE**        | [Common Applications Kept Enhanced](https://www.bufferbloat.net/projects/codel/wiki/Cake/). Network AQM algorithm this scheduler adapts. |
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2625:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:631:| **Direct Dispatch** | `SCX_DSQ_LOCAL_ON` — task goes directly to a CPU's local queue, bypassing the DSQ path. |
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2626:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:1:<img src="logo.png" alt="scx_chaos" width="60%">
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2627:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:3:A general purpose `sched_ext` scheduler designed to amplify race conditions for testing and debugging.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2628:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:7:`scx_chaos` is a specialized scheduler that intentionally introduces various forms of latency and performance degradation to help expose race conditions and timing-dependent bugs in applications. Unlike traditional schedulers that aim for optimal performance, `scx_chaos` is designed to stress-test applications by introducing controlled chaos into the scheduling process.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2629:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:9:**WARNING**: This scheduler is experimental and should not be used in production environments. It is specifically designed to degrade performance and may cause system instability.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2630:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:13:The scheduler supports several "chaos traits" that can be enabled individually or in combination, with more to come:
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2631:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:47:sudo scx_chaos
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2632:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:53:sudo scx_chaos --random-delay-frequency 0.1 --random-delay-min-us 100 --random-delay-max-us 1000
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2633:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:59:sudo scx_chaos --cpufreq-frequency 0.2 --cpufreq-min 400000 --cpufreq-max 2000000
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2634:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:65:sudo scx_chaos --degradation-frequency 0.15 --degradation-frac7 64
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2635:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:71:sudo scx_chaos --kprobes-for-random-delays schedule do_exit --kprobe-random-delay-frequency 0.05 --kprobe-random-delay-min-us 50 --kprobe-random-delay-max-us 500
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2636:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:76:Run a specific command under the chaos scheduler:
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2637:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:79:sudo scx_chaos [chaos-options] -- ./your-application --app-args
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2638:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:82:The scheduler will automatically detach when the application exits.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2639:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:89:sudo scx_chaos --pid 1234 [chaos-options]
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2640:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:97:sudo scx_chaos --stats 1.0 [chaos-options]  # Update every 1 second
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2641:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:100:Run in monitoring mode only (no scheduler):
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2642:./scheds/rust/scx_chaos/README.md:103:sudo scx_chaos --monitor 2.0
