./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4901:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2592:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:61:Traditional schedulers (CFS, EEVDF) optimize for **fairness** — if a game and a compiler both run, each gets 50% CPU time. For gaming, this creates two problems:
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4902:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2593:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:66:**scx_cake's answer**: Detect the game process family automatically (Steam, Wine/Proton, native games) and give it scheduling priority. Non-game tasks are classified by PELT CPU utilization into NORMAL, HOG, or BG classes with progressively lower priority. The system self-tunes — no manual configuration needed.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4903:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2594:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:68:This is the same insight behind network CAKE: short flows (DNS, gaming packets) should not be delayed by bulk flows (downloads). scx_cake applies this to CPU time.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4904:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2595:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:74:`scx_cake` classifies every task into one of four classes. Classification uses PELT (Per-Entity Load Tracking) utilization from the kernel and automatic game family detection via process tree analysis.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4905:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2596:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:91:2. **PELT-based classification**: Every 64th stop, the scheduler reads the kernel's `util_avg` for each task. Tasks with ≥78% CPU utilization are classified as HOG; lower-utilization non-game tasks become BG during GAMING state, or NORMAL otherwise.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4906:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2597:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:139:scx_cake uses a virtual runtime system inspired by EEVDF:
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4907:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2598:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:142:- **Nice scaling**: Per-task `nice_shift` (0-12) scales runtime cost. High `nice` priority → less vruntime cost → dispatches sooner. Computed once per 64 stops from `p->scx.weight`.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4908:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2599:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:155:        SELECT["cake_select_cpu<br/>3-gate + tunnel"] --> |GATE 1| PREV["prev_cpu idle?<br/>scx_bpf_test_and_clear_cpu_idle"]
