./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4913:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2604:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:249:`select_cpu` caches `scx_bpf_now()` in per-CPU BSS (`cpu_bss[cpu].cached_now`). `enqueue` reuses this value, saving ~15ns (1 kfunc trampoline entry) on the all-busy path.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4914:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2605:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:262:3. **Preempt decision**: If `elapsed >= vprot_ns` → `scx_bpf_kick_cpu(victim, SCX_KICK_PREEMPT)`. Otherwise → suppressed (counted as `nr_vprot_suppressed` in stats).
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4915:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2606:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:275:The clock domain fix in `cake_running` (using `scx_bpf_now()` instead of `p->se.exec_start`) prevents a subtle starvation bug: after ~22 minutes, accumulated IRQ time drift in `exec_start` would exceed the u32 wrap boundary, corrupting elapsed-time checks and causing unconditional preemption (priority inversion).
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:4916:docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:2607:./scheds/rust/scx_cake/README.md:347:1. **Warmup**: 1 second pause for the scheduler to stabilize
