./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:5370:docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:738:scheds/rust/scx_pandemonium/README.md:7:PANDEMONIUM is included in the [sched-ext/scx](https://github.com/sched-ext/scx) project alongside scx_rusty, scx_lavd, scx_cosmos, scx_cake and the rest of the sched_ext family. Thank you to Piotr Gorski and the sched-ext team. PANDEMONIUM is made possible by contributions from the sched_ext, CachyOS, Gentoo, OpenSUSE, Arch and Ubuntu communities within the Linux ecosystem.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:5371:docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:739:scheds/rust/scx_pandemonium/README.md:11:12 AMD Zen CPUs, kernel 6.18+, clang 21. The tables below report v5.8.0 PANDEMONIUM numbers from a single-iteration bench-scale run across 2C/4C/8C/12C; the v5.9.0 deltas at 12C are summarized in the next subsection. EEVDF and scx_bpfland baselines are best-3-of-N historical (28 and 26 complete runs across 75 bench-scale sessions) — those baselines don't drift across PANDEMONIUM versions. v5.8.0 closed the 2C structural starvation class via the rescue-fairness fix and the missing CPU-bound demotion in stopping() that was leaving long-runners stuck at TIER_INTERACTIVE (longrun WORST 19s -> 13ms at 2C, mixed WORST 29s -> 16ms at 2C). Bench-fork-thread lands within 1% of EEVDF and ~40% ahead of scx_bpfland.
./docs/missions/lavd-docs-services-audit.log:5372:docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:740:scheds/rust/scx_pandemonium/README.md:29:| Cores | EEVDF    | scx_bpfland | PANDEMONIUM (BPF) | PANDEMONIUM (ADAPTIVE) |
