./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:730:docs/missions/audio-boost-review.log:1124:- Audio polling updates the pinned map independently of focus events. The audio thread polls `sample_audio()` and calls `g.update_audio(set)` directly at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:577](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:577) and [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:589](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:589). `update_audio()` rebuilds audio state and immediately calls `apply_active_keys()` at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:200](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:200), which performs the actual pinned-map deletes/inserts at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:205](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:205).
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:731:docs/missions/audio-boost-review.log:1126:- Browser-mode updates preserve active audio PIDs. `BoostState` tracks `base_keys` separately from `audio_pids` at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:81](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:81), and `rebuild()` unions both sets at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:115](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:115). `update_browser()` only replaces the base focus/tab set, then applies the rebuilt union at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:167](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:167).
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:732:docs/missions/audio-boost-review.log:1128:Remaining risk/test gap: the added tests cover the `BoostState` union behavior at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:467](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:467) and [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:482](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:482), but there is no mocked or integration test proving `update_audio()` actually reconciles `last_keys` into the pinned map. Also, if `pactl` fails to spawn after audio PIDs were previously recorded, the error path logs but does not clear stale audio PIDs until a later successful poll returns an empty set.
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:733:docs/missions/audio-boost-review.log:1135:- Audio polling updates the pinned map independently of focus events. The audio thread polls `sample_audio()` and calls `g.update_audio(set)` directly at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:577](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:577) and [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:589](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:589). `update_audio()` rebuilds audio state and immediately calls `apply_active_keys()` at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:200](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:200), which performs the actual pinned-map deletes/inserts at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:205](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:205).
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:734:docs/missions/audio-boost-review.log:1137:- Browser-mode updates preserve active audio PIDs. `BoostState` tracks `base_keys` separately from `audio_pids` at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:81](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:81), and `rebuild()` unions both sets at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:115](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:115). `update_browser()` only replaces the base focus/tab set, then applies the rebuilt union at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:167](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:167).
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:735:docs/missions/audio-boost-review.log:1139:Remaining risk/test gap: the added tests cover the `BoostState` union behavior at [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:467](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:467) and [anima_hypr_daemon.rs:482](/home/vi/animaschedext/scheds/rust/scx_lavd/examples/anima_hypr_daemon.rs:482), but there is no mocked or integration test proving `update_audio()` actually reconciles `last_keys` into the pinned map. Also, if `pactl` fails to spawn after audio PIDs were previously recorded, the error path logs but does not clear stale audio PIDs until a later successful poll returns an empty set.
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:736:scheds/experimental/scx_wd40/README.md:1:# scx_wd40
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:737:scheds/experimental/scx_wd40/README.md:3:An experimental fork of the `scx_rusty` scheduler that uses BPF arenas to simplify scheduler development. Found in the main [`sched_ext`](https://github.com/sched-ext/scx/tree/main) repository. [Read more about `sched_ext`](https://github.com/sched-ext/scx/tree/main).
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:738:scheds/rust/scx_pandemonium/README.md:7:PANDEMONIUM is included in the [sched-ext/scx](https://github.com/sched-ext/scx) project alongside scx_rusty, scx_lavd, scx_cosmos, scx_cake and the rest of the sched_ext family. Thank you to Piotr Gorski and the sched-ext team. PANDEMONIUM is made possible by contributions from the sched_ext, CachyOS, Gentoo, OpenSUSE, Arch and Ubuntu communities within the Linux ecosystem.
./docs/missions/lavd-scope-audit.log:739:scheds/rust/scx_pandemonium/README.md:11:12 AMD Zen CPUs, kernel 6.18+, clang 21. The tables below report v5.8.0 PANDEMONIUM numbers from a single-iteration bench-scale run across 2C/4C/8C/12C; the v5.9.0 deltas at 12C are summarized in the next subsection. EEVDF and scx_bpfland baselines are best-3-of-N historical (28 and 26 complete runs across 75 bench-scale sessions) — those baselines don't drift across PANDEMONIUM versions. v5.8.0 closed the 2C structural starvation class via the rescue-fairness fix and the missing CPU-bound demotion in stopping() that was leaving long-runners stuck at TIER_INTERACTIVE (longrun WORST 19s -> 13ms at 2C, mixed WORST 29s -> 16ms at 2C). Bench-fork-thread lands within 1% of EEVDF and ~40% ahead of scx_bpfland.
